# sudoers rule for the Xymon "claude" extension.
#
# The extension reports how long the Claude Code login of an account is
# still valid. That information sits in $HOME/.claude/.credentials.json,
# mode 0600 in a private home directory, so the unprivileged Xymon
# client cannot read it. claude-expiry.sh is the only part that needs
# root: it takes a USER NAME (never a path), reads that account's
# credentials file and prints the two expiry timestamps and the
# subscription type - no token material, ever.
#
# Install this file with visudo -f:
#
#   Linux (Debian/Ubuntu):  visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/xymon-claude
#   Linux (Rocky/EL):       visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/xymon-claude
#   FreeBSD:                visudo -f /usr/local/etc/sudoers.d/xymon-claude
#
# Keep exactly one uncommented line per account and platform. The user
# name is part of the rule on purpose: sudo then permits exactly the
# accounts named here and nothing else, so the rule cannot be turned
# into a way of reading other files as root.
#
# Hosts where the Xymon client itself runs as root (or where the
# standalone runner runs from root's crontab, as on OpenWrt) need no
# rule at all - set CLAUDE_SUDO="no" in claude.cfg there.

# Debian/Ubuntu and Rocky/EL - the default account:
xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh root

# Rocky/EL with the EPEL xymon-client package (different prefix):
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/share/xymon-client/ext/claude-expiry.sh root

# FreeBSD (net-mgmt/xymon-client):
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/www/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh root

# Further accounts: one line per account, and add the account to
# CLAUDE_ACCOUNTS in claude.cfg. Example for a service account "deploy"
# and a user "alice" on Debian/Ubuntu:
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh deploy
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh alice
#
# Several accounts in one line work as well:
#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh root, /usr/lib/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh deploy
#
# Do NOT write a rule without the argument, e.g.
#   xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/xymon/client/ext/claude-expiry.sh
# That allows ANY argument, i.e. every account on the host.
